Question 2
Write an R program to accept a positive integer n and determine whether it is even or odd, divisible by 3 and 5, prime, or palindrome. Use appropriate relational and logical operators along with decision-making statements.

Code:
n <- as.integer(readline("Enter number: "))

if (n %% 2 == 0) print("Even") else print("Odd")

if (n %% 3 == 0 && n %% 5 == 0)
  print("Divisible by 3 and 5")
else print("Not divisible by both")

p <- TRUE
if (n <= 1) p <- FALSE
if (n > 2) {
  for (i in 2:(n-1))
    if (n %% i == 0) p <- FALSE
}

if (p) print("Prime") else print("Not Prime")

r <- as.integer(paste(rev(strsplit(as.character(n), "")[[1]]), collapse=""))

if (n == r) print("Palindrome") else print("Not Palindrome")
