Question 5
Write an R program to accept a positive integer and, using a while loop:

a. Count the number of digits.
b. Find the sum of its digits.
c. Reverse the number.
d. Check whether it is a palindrome.

Code:
n <- as.integer(readline("Enter a positive integer: "))

temp <- n
count <- 0
sum <- 0
rev <- 0

while (temp > 0) {
  digit <- temp %% 10

  count <- count + 1
  sum <- sum + digit
  rev <- rev * 10 + digit

  temp <- temp %/% 10
}

print(paste("Number of digits =", count))
print(paste("Sum of digits =", sum))
print(paste("Reverse =", rev))

if (n == rev)
  print("Palindrome")
else
  print("Not Palindrome")
